Green Haven Dog Rescue Website
A responsive multi-page web application built for Green Haven Dog Rescue, a Non-Profit Organisation (NPO) dedicated to rescuing, rehabilitating, and rehoming domestic animals across the Western Cape, South Africa.

Project Features
Responsive Layout: Mobile-friendly design using CSS Grid, Flexbox, and media queries.

Hero Banner: Custom hero section with background overlays and quick-action Call-To-Action (CTA) buttons.

Core Pillars Grid: Visual showcase highlighting Rescue & Rehabilitation, Spay & Neuter Clinics, and Community Awareness.

Comprehensive Navigation & Footer: Accessible header navigation paired with a multi-column footer containing quick links, contact information, legal disclosures, and social media links.

Floating Quick-Action Buttons: Fixed-position quick-access buttons for direct WhatsApp messaging, emergency phone calls, and adoption enquiries.

Repository Structure
Plaintext
.
├── CSS/
│   └── style.css            # Main stylesheet for global layout and components
├── Images/
│   ├── Home Screen.webp     # Hero banner background image
│   └── logo.png             # Site header brand logo
├── Pages/
│   ├── about.html           # Information regarding mission, vision, and team
│   ├── contactus.html       # Contact form, location maps, and operating hours
│   ├── enquiry.html         # Adoption, fostering, and volunteer enquiry forms
│   └── services.html        # Detailed breakdown of rescue and community programs
└── index.html               # Homepage entry point
Tech Stack
HTML5: Semantic structural layout and ARIA accessibility labels.

CSS3: Custom CSS variables (:root), Flexbox, CSS Grid layouts, and custom media queries.

Getting Started
Clone or download the repository:

Bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/green-haven-dog-rescue.git
Navigate to the project folder:

Bash
cd green-haven-dog-rescue
Open index.html in your web browser of choice, or run it using a local development server (such as Visual Studio Code's Live Server extension).
